    2. Place guide bar at position with >=5 cells on each side; choose coverage 70-100% starting from index 0, with 0-2 internal gaps of size 1-3
    3. Build output adjacency pattern; for each guide pixel, decide if side-A and/or side-B get a source pixel (total 6-12 output source pixels, at least 2 per side)
    4. For each output source pixel, scatter 1-2 input source pixels on the same side at random distances (>=2) along the same perpendicular line; this naturally produces valid projections and merges
    5. Add erased sources by placing pixels on gap columns/rows or outside the guide span (3-7 of these ensure non-trivial filtering)
